{"repo":"mercadona/control-tower","epic":"\"9\"","issue":329,"plan":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-issue-329-gate-1-the-freeze.md","plan_sha256":"58436bf0b58bc9c41ad5b0d4c82f6386ca6a96503f08606696d1e3f2e55a498e","task":3,"task_name":"The epic's branch: committed, pushed, never the default","tasks_total":13,"step":"implement","attempt":1,"plugin_version":"0.57.0","actor":"jponzvan@mercadona.es","written_at":"2026-09-14T10:55:16.587Z","outcome":"done","paths":6,"why":null,"summary":"Added the EpicBranch port and its GitEpicBranch adapter: current() reads the checkout's branch, publish() refuses with EpicBranchNotPublished before any write when that branch equals the remote's declared default, otherwise adds, commits and pushes it and answers the branch. Extracted GitWorkspace's default-branch parsing into the public static declaredBranchIn(printed), which both GitWorkspace#declaredBase and GitEpicBranch now call, so the decision of what the remote's default branch is stays in one place. Wired EpicBranchNotPublished and EpicBranchNotUnderstood into start-plan-route.ts's PlanCollapse with kebab-case codes epic-branch-not-published and epic-branch-not-understood. TDD skill loaded without error; the red test (checkout on the branch the remote calls default) was verified failing on a missing module first, and I additionally mutated the publish() equality guard by hand to confirm that test dies for the stated reason before restoring the file byte-for-byte. All three verification commands pass (typecheck, git-epic-branch + git-workspace, plan-refusal), and the whole fast backend suite (68 files, 1574 tests) stays green. Note for the reviewer: EpicBranch has no production caller yet inside this task's scope (start-plan-route.ts only gained the refusal mapping) — later tasks of this same plan (5 and 6) wire GitEpicBranch into gate 1's press, which is outside this task's Files line.","brief_vara_ct_docs":8,"brief_bytes":56665,"agent_bytes":11986,"skill_bytes":18145,"package