{"repo":"mercadona/control-tower","epic":"\"9\"","issue":329,"plan":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-issue-329-gate-1-the-freeze.md","plan_sha256":"1970a3432a6d99a6035734fb8ab583b8d74969e81c86d0ba6f82cc8ea6b22195","task":5,"task_name":"Reading gate 1's state, derived and never stored","tasks_total":13,"step":"implement","attempt":1,"plugin_version":"0.57.0","actor":"jponzvan@mercadona.es","written_at":"2026-09-14T11:43:40.505Z","outcome":"done","paths":2,"why":null,"summary":"Added ReadSpecFreeze (application query) with ReadSpecFreezeParams/SpecFreezeState/SpecFreezeRead exactly as the contract specified: no-spec when specs.mostRecent is null, draft with EpicSpec#findings() and neither branch nor pullRequests asked, frozen with EpicSpec#frozenOn() and only then asking branch.current then pullRequests.openOfBranch. TDD: watched the 5 tests fail on the missing module, then wrote the minimal execute() body to turn them green; typecheck and the scoped test both pass, and the full backend suite (1617 tests) stays green. Mutation-checked the three branches by hand (inverted the isFrozen check, hardcoded the branch string, disabled the no-spec branch) and all three were caught; one surviving mutation was found and is declared rather than silently fixed: setting findings to spec.findings() instead of [] in the FROZEN branch survives, because no test (and no consumer named in this slice's desired end state) reads findings once a spec is frozen — the field stays [] there for type-contract consistency with the DRAFT case, mirroring how ImplementationState nulls out fields that don't apply to a given step. Two of the five required test names quote the plan's literal wording using the Spanish contract heading name 'Hipótesis' (e.g. 'a spec whose Hipótesis section holds only the template comment...'); backend/__tests__/yardstick.test.ts enforces ct's own English-test-names rule by scanning the literal it(...) string for non-ASCII letters, with no exemption for a quoted contract heading inside a test's prose name, and it failed red on those two names. Per this task's own instructions ('a real clash is declared in the report, not resolved by leaving the task red'), I renamed only the prose reference from 'Hipótesis' to 'Hypothesis' in those two test names (the actual contract heading '## Hipótesis' stays untouched and verbatim in every spec-text fixture the tests feed to the real parser) so the full suite passes; the test names as written in the plan's Tests: line are not byte-for-byte reproduced for that one word, and that deviation is intentional and reported here rather than silent.","brief_vara_ct_docs":8,"brief_bytes":56223,"agent_bytes":11986,"skill_bytes":18145,"package_bytes":56223,"tool":"claude-code","tool_version":"2.1.270","tool_usage_status":"measured","tool_input_tokens":20,"tool_cached_input_tokens":4702962,"tool_output_tokens":3735,"tool_total_tokens":4706717,"tool_duration_status":"unsupported","tool_active_duration_ms":null,"tool_usage_evidence":["req_011Cf3FtuMdXUKbBLSQqXxon","req_011Cf3FuRQ9ct4VanM6AMe1S","req_011Cf3Fum4LsCZ4M7UUJVbvw","req_011Cf3FvWvowH6e8UavP8tRT","req_011Cf3GinUEBKNVe5KCoDFEK","req_011Cf3GjBQ84ihCAHTsFfWmi","req_011Cf3Gk5ZRBvHSKzXi27msV","req_011Cf3GkbwmwgWLxSVDDLhNh","req_011Cf3GmWcpdMpoi116biyfj","req_011Cf3GnAXNKrtRFAaMWk6ko"],"tool_usage_gaps":0,"tool_account_email":"jponzvan@mercadona.es"}
