{"repo":"mercadona/control-tower","epic":"\"9\"","issue":329,"plan":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-issue-329-gate-1-the-freeze.md","plan_sha256":"29a11254c913daaf1f4d0006b76cffb447b3d93619b50555e751e23a725c554a","task":7,"task_name":"The read of gate 1, and the key only the page gets","tasks_total":13,"step":"implement","attempt":1,"plugin_version":"0.57.0","actor":"jponzvan@mercadona.es","written_at":"2026-09-14T12:35:56.726Z","outcome":"done","paths":3,"why":null,"summary":"GateKey mints one hex key at construction from an injected random function and reveals it via forThePage only when Browsers.isOurOwnPage(origin, host) holds, reusing that existing check rather than reimplementing D-22's boundary; holds(offered) does strict equality against the minted key for the POST side task 8 will add. SpecFreezeRoute.reading answers none/no-spec/draft/frozen straight off CoordinatingSessions.held() and ReadSpecFreeze, projecting spec to its EpicSpec#path and each finding to a plain {code, line, detail}, with the key field included only when GateKey.forThePage minted one for this request's Origin/Host. Tested through a real listening server built locally in the test (a small express app mounting just this route), since api-server.ts is not wired to /spec-freeze until task 9 and ApiServer cannot yet serve this path. Verified both the D-22 boundary and the no-coordinating-session short-circuit by mutating the implementation by hand, watching the suite go red for the expected reason, and restoring the file. Both verification commands pass (typecheck exit 0, the 5 named tests exit 0), and the full fast backend suite (71 files, 1612 tests) stays green.","brief_vara_ct_docs":8,"brief_bytes":55919,"agent_bytes":11986,"skill_bytes":18145,"package_bytes":55919,"tool":"claude-code","tool_version":"2.1.270","tool_usage_status":"measured","tool_input_tokens":12,"tool_cached_input_tokens":2984150,"tool_output_tokens":2680,"tool_total_tokens":2986842,"tool_duration_status":"unsupporte