{"repo":"mercadona/control-tower","epic":"\"9\"","issue":329,"plan":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-issue-329-gate-1-the-freeze.md","plan_sha256":"29a11254c913daaf1f4d0006b76cffb447b3d93619b50555e751e23a725c554a","task":8,"task_name":"The press of gate 1, refused to anything that is not the page","tasks_total":13,"step":"implement","attempt":1,"plugin_version":"0.57.0","actor":"jponzvan@mercadona.es","written_at":"2026-09-14T12:54:55.012Z","outcome":"done","paths":3,"why":null,"summary":"POST /spec-freeze checks GateKey.HEADER first and refuses 403 gate-not-from-the-page without ever calling FreezeSpec.execute, then 400 no-coordinating-session, then runs the freeze and projects its FreezeOutcome through a new SpecFreezeRefusal (a Projection, one file with SpecFreezeRoute per architecture.md's one-controller-per-endpoint) to no-epic-spec, spec-already-frozen and spec-not-freezable, the last naming the first finding's line or code; a PlanFailure from the freeze reuses the PlanCollapse already wired for EpicSpecNotUnderstood and its siblings, no new entry needed there. FROZEN answers 200 with only status/on/pullRequest, deliberately narrower than the GET route's frozen body (no spec path) per the task's own contract. refusal-codes.test.ts now folds SpecFreezeOutcome into the request-vocabulary sweep; no code collided with another vocabulary. The wording of the no-coordinating-session, no-epic-spec and spec-already-frozen refusal details was not pinned by the brief (only spec-not-freezable's exact format was), so I picked plain text consistent with the file's tone — worth a look if the frontend panel expects specific copy. Verified by hand-mutating four lines one at a time (the gate-key check, the no-coordinating-session guard, the finding count in the not-freezable detail, and the frozen body's on/pullRequest fields) and watching the exact test each protects go red for that reason, then restoring; both verification commands pass (typecheck exit 0, the two test files exit 0 with 13 tests), and the full fast backend suite stays green (71 files, 1617 tests).","brief_vara_ct_docs":8,"brief_bytes":55757,"agent_bytes":11986,"skill_bytes":18145,"package_bytes":55757,"tool":"claude-code","tool_version":"2.1.270","tool_usage_status":"measured","tool_input_tokens":10,"tool_cached_input_tokens":2536969,"tool_output_tokens":3539,"tool_total_tokens":2540518,"tool_duration_status":"unsupported","tool_active_duration_ms":null,"tool_usage_evidence":["req_011Cf3MKurRmFsYf8s76BtMB","req_011Cf3MLe3C8pa3u9h8YcrXF","req_011Cf3MMjJyQBgLKwrtMSG7s","req_011Cf3NBUeWEr3NKVkJYxPAf","req_011Cf3NBk6gt3Rj46387go49"],"tool_usage_gaps":0,"tool_account_email":"jponzvan@mercadona.es"}
